## 2. Scholarly grounding pipeline (mandatory)

**Discover in vectors / Athanor, cite from Ahmes nodes.** See [`grounding/README.md`](./grounding/README.md).

Prefer the evidence matrix in [`grounding/README.md`](./grounding/README.md) (unit IDs I.1–I.9 / II.1–II.6). The temario harvest ([`grounding/temario/PROVENANCE-LAYER.md`](./grounding/temario/PROVENANCE-LAYER.md)) is a coverage demo — **do not paste its T1 index-page quote**. Promote only the matrix Tri-Anchors. Never paste DevIAC/Athanor `content_preview` into lessons.

```bash
cd ~/src/deviac && make ingest-profield-dc   # when corpus refreshes
# optional field index: athanor search … --project-slug profield-digital-creativity --vault scholar
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8100/vectors/search \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query":"<unit topic>","project_slug":"profield-digital-creativity","knowledge_scope":"field_prospection","n_results":5}'
# then: ahmes query --cite "$DB:<node_id>" --style chicago-author-date
```

Cite `⟨coat⟩ · nodo ⟨id⟩ · p. ⟨n⟩`. If evidence matrix says NONE → declared-gap paragraph.

### 2.1 Athanor-assisted forge ignitor

Before writing B1–B3, run one short, unit-scoped Athanor query against
`project_slug=profield-digital-creativity` and
`knowledge_scope=field_prospection`. Treat its result as a **discovery pointer**
with four recorded fields: query text, source locator, similarity, and proposed
unit use. Then resolve the candidate in Ahmes:

```text
Athanor candidate → source hash / document → Ahmes extraction.db
→ complete node + page → ahmes query --cite → evaluator_safe gate
→ lesson claim, or explicit [BIBLIO-GAP]/NONE
```

Ignitor query seeds:

| Unit family | Query seed | Forge decision |
| --- | --- | --- |
| I.1–I.4 | `fashion design education AI visualization process assessment` | Make iteration and critique observable; do not infer Photoshop pedagogy from an AI study. |
| I.5–I.6 | `fashion spatial visualization 3D volume teaching CLO` | Diagnose spatial reasoning separately from package operation; generic mesh/CSG transfer requires evidence. |
| II.1–II.2 | `fashion image synthesis ethics avatar authorship student process` | Require process/provenance and human judgement; keep VTON out of scope. |
| II.3/II.6 | `fashion digital exhibition student experience object based learning` | Separate experience/staging evidence from evidence of a teaching method. |
| II.4 | `fashion video education studio production process` | Make storyboard → capture → edit → critique → export traceable. |
| II.5 | `generative AI studio based fashion education authorship ethics` | Add authorship/material/tool declarations and human verification to the portfolio forge. |

Verified examples from the current corpus:

- Anwar, Raza & Marzouk (2025), *Generative AI in Studio-Based Fashion
  Education*: Ahmes node `0d5bfc56-5325-5145-9f76-82f4650d7bdb`, p.2,
  `(Anwar 2025, 2)`, `evaluator_safe=yes`. Use for authorship/studio-process
  framing, not as proof that a particular tool sequence improves learning.
- Smith-Glaviana (2025), *University Students’ Experience of a Digital Fashion
  Exhibition*: Ahmes node `19f2e4c6-34e6-599a-8b5c-87a01bc08900`, p.1,
  `(Smith-Glaviana 2025, 1)`, `evaluator_safe=yes`. Use for experience and
  object-based-learning context, not as a validated AR teaching method.

The current index also returns malformed AI-fashion metadata with a
host-title mismatch. That result is a useful retrieval warning, not evidence:
quarantine it, retain `[BIBLIO-GAP]`, and never promote its preview into a CV or
lesson. Athanor is therefore an adaptive question-and-routing layer; Ahmes is
the citation boundary.

